    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline now emits an audit line after the owner is saved.\n\n**New function step** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n```java\nprivate static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n\npublic void service(@Val Owner owner) {\n    AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n}\n```\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond` (kept under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbours):\n```yaml\nsave:\n  ...\n  next: audit\naudit:\n  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.AuditOwnerCreated\n  govern: [ transaction ]\n  next: respond\n```\n\nIt runs after `SaveOwner` so the owner id is assigned, and the logged line carries the id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` \u2014 verified in the run output:\n\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-04\n```\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
